 "title": "Score Bands: Reliability and Validity of IQ-Style Tests",
 "tagline": "Turn a test score into a range, simulate retests, and quiz yourself on what reliability and validity mean.",
 "lead": "An IQ-style score, such as one from a Wechsler-type test, looks like one exact number. Every test has some measurement error, so the honest answer is a range. Use the calculators, the simulation and the quiz to see how much the result can move and why.",
