 "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Score Bands: Reliability and Validity</title>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#f7f7fb;--card:#fff;--fg:#1d1f2b;--muted:#5b6072;--line:#d9dbe5;--acc:#3b5bdb;--acc2:#e8590c;--ok:#2b8a3e;--bad:#c92a2a;--band:rgba(59,91,219,.18);--grid:#e6e8f0}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:#12141c;--card:#1b1e29;--fg:#e8eaf2;--muted:#a3a8bb;--line:#30344a;--acc:#7c9bff;--acc2:#ff9a5c;--ok:#69db7c;--bad:#ff8787;--band:rgba(124,155,255,.22);--grid:#272b3c}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nbody{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif}\nheader{padding:20px 16px 8px;max-width:860px;margin:auto}\nh1{font-size:1.45rem;margin:0 0 6px}\nh2{font-size:1.2rem;margin:0 0 8px}\nh3{font-size:1rem;margin:16px 0 6px}\np{margin:6px 0}\n.muted{color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem}\nnav{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;max-width:860px;margin:8px auto 0;padding:0 16px}\nnav button{flex:1;min-width:90px;padding:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--card);color:var(--fg);border-radius:10px;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}\nnav button[aria-selected=true]{background:var(--acc);color:#fff;border-color:var(--acc)}\nmain{max-width:860px;margin:auto;padding:12px 16px 40px}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:16px;margin:12px 0}\n.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:12px}\nlabel{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:4px}\ninput[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:var(--acc)}\ninput[type=number],select{width:100%;padding:8px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:inherit}\n.val{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--acc);font-weight:700}\n.big{font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:800;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:10px}\n.stat{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:10px;background:var(--bg)}\n.stat b{display:block;font-size:1.25rem;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.stat span{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}\nsvg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}\ncanvas{width:100%;display:block;border-radius:10px;background:var(--bg);touch-action:pan-y}\n.plots{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:12px}\n.btn{padding:10px 14px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--acc);background:var(--acc);color:#fff;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}\n.btn.alt{background:transparent;color:var(--acc)}\nbutton:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--acc2);outline-offset:2px}\nfieldset{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:12px;margin:10px 0}\nlegend{font-weight:700;padding:0 4px}\n.opt{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;padding:6px;border-radius:8px;font-weight:400;cursor:pointer}\n.opt:hover{background:var(--bg)}\n.opt input{margin-top:5px}\n.fb{margin-top:6px;font-size:.93rem}\n.fb.ok{color:var(--ok)}.fb.bad{color:var(--bad)}\n.hidden{display:none}\nul{padding-left:20px;margin:6px 0}\nli{margin:4px 0}\n.note{border-left:4px solid var(--acc2);padding:6px 10px;background:var(--bg);border-radius:6px;font-size:.92rem}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header>\n<h1>Score Bands: Reliability and Validity</h1>\n<p class=\"muted\">IQ-style tests, such as the Wechsler scales, report scores with an average of 100. About two thirds of people score between 85 and 115. This page uses a simple model. It has no real test items and no real norms.</p>\n</header>\n<nav role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Sections\">\n<button role=\"tab\" id=\"t-num\" aria-controls=\"p-num\" aria-selected=\"true\">🔢 Numerize</button>\n<button role=\"tab\" id=\"t-gr\" aria-controls=\"p-gr\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">📈 Graph</button>\n<button role=\"tab\" id=\"t-qz\" aria-controls=\"p-qz\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">📝 Test</button>\n</nav>\n<main>\n\n<section id=\"p-num\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"t-num\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<h2>From one number to a range</h2>\n<p><b>Reliability</b> means how consistent a score is. It runs from 0 (pure noise) to 1 (no error).</p>\n<p>The <b>standard error of measurement (SEM)</b> is the typical size of the error. SEM = 15 × √(1 − reliability).</p>\n<div class=\"row\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">\n<div><label for=\"sc\">Observed score: <span class=\"val\" id=\"scv\">115</span></label>\n<input type=\"range\" id=\"sc\" min=\"40\" max=\"160\" value=\"115\" step=\"1\"></div>\n<div><label for=\"rel\">Reliability: <span class=\"val\" id=\"relv\">0.90</span></label>\n<input type=\"range\" id=\"rel\" min=\"0.50\" max=\"0.99\" value=\"0.90\" step=\"0.01\"></div>\n<div><label for=\"conf\">Confidence level</label>\n<select id=\"conf\"><option value=\"1\">68% (about 1 SEM)</option><option value=\"1.645\">90%</option><option value=\"1.96\" selected>95%</option></select></div>\n</div>\n<svg id=\"curve\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 190\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"curveDesc\"><desc id=\"curveDesc\">Bell curve of scores from 40 to 160 with the score range shaded.</desc></svg>\n<div class=\"stats\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"o-sem\">–</b><span>SEM (typical error)</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"o-band\">–</b><span>Simple range: score ± z × SEM</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"o-true\">–</b><span>Estimated true score</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"o-band2\">–</b><span>Range around estimated true score</span></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">The <b>true score</b> is the average you would get over many error-free tries. It sits a bit closer to 100 than the observed score. This pull toward the average is called <b>regression to the mean</b>.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"card\">\n<h2>Is the gap between two index scores real?</h2>\n<p>Tests often split into parts called <b>index scores</b> (for example, verbal and memory). A gap between two parts may be just error.</p>\n<div class=\"row\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">\n<div><label for=\"ia\">Index A score</label><input type=\"number\" id=\"ia\" min=\"40\" max=\"160\" value=\"108\"></div>\n<div><label for=\"ib\">Index B score</label><input type=\"number\" id=\"ib\" min=\"40\" max=\"160\" value=\"96\"></div>\n<div><label for=\"ra\">Reliability of A: <span class=\"val\" id=\"rav\">0.90</span></label><input type=\"range\" id=\"ra\" min=\"0.50\" max=\"0.99\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.90\"></div>\n<div><label for=\"rb\">Reliability of B: <span class=\"val\" id=\"rbv\">0.88</span></label><input type=\"range\" id=\"rb\" min=\"0.50\" max=\"0.99\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.88\"></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"stats\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"d-gap\">–</b><span>Gap (A − B)</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"d-crit\">–</b><span>Gap needed at 95%</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"d-res\">–</b><span>Verdict</span></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"note\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">“Bigger than error” is not the same as “rare”. Many people in the general population have gaps of this size. A gap only means something when it fits other evidence.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"p-gr\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"t-gr\" class=\"hidden\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<h2>Simulate 2,000 people</h2>\n<p>Each simulated person has a true ability. They take the test twice. We also measure a later real-world outcome, like school grades.</p>\n<div class=\"row\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">\n<div><label for=\"g-r\">Test reliability: <span class=\"val\" id=\"g-rv\">0.90</span></label><input type=\"range\" id=\"g-r\" min=\"0.30\" max=\"0.99\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.90\"></div>\n<div><label for=\"g-v\">True link to outcome: <span class=\"val\" id=\"g-vv\">0.60</span></label><input type=\"range\" id=\"g-v\" min=\"0\" max=\"0.95\" step=\"0.05\" value=\"0.60\"></div>\n<div><label for=\"g-y\">Outcome reliability: <span class=\"val\" id=\"g-yv\">0.80</span></label><input type=\"range\" id=\"g-y\" min=\"0.30\" max=\"1\" step=\"0.05\" value=\"0.80\"></div>\n</div>\n<p style=\"margin-top:10px\"><button class=\"btn alt\" id=\"g-new\">🎲 New random sample</button></p>\n<div class=\"plots\">\n<figure style=\"margin:0\"><canvas id=\"c1\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scatter plot: first test against retest\"></canvas><figcaption class=\"muted\">Reliability: test vs. retest. The dashed line means “same score twice”.</figcaption></figure>\n<figure style=\"margin:0\"><canvas id=\"c2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scatter plot: test score against outcome\"></canvas><figcaption class=\"muted\">Validity: test vs. outcome.</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n<div class=\"stats\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"s-rr\">–</b><span>Test–retest correlation</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"s-cat\">–</b><span>Changed band on retest (below 85 / 85–114 / 115+)</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"s-130\">–</b><span>Scored 130+ first, and 130+ again</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"s-val\">–</b><span>Observed test–outcome correlation</span></div>\n<div class=\"stat\"><b id=\"s-exp\">–</b><span>Expected: link × √(rel × outcome rel)</span></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">A <b>correlation</b> runs from −1 to 1. Higher means the dots form a tighter line. Error in either measure makes the observed link weaker than the true link. This is called <b>attenuation</b>.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"card\">\n<h2>Points to think about</h2>\n<h3>Kinds of reliability</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Test–retest:</b> do people get similar scores on two dates?</li>\n<li><b>Internal consistency:</b> do the items inside a test agree with each other?</li>\n<li>Big combined scores use many items. They are usually more reliable than small subtests.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Kinds of validity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Content:</b> do the tasks cover the skill they claim to cover?</li>\n<li><b>Construct:</b> does the score behave like the idea behind it should?</li>\n<li><b>Criterion:</b> does the score relate to outcomes like grades or job tasks?</li>\n<li>Validity is about a use, not the test alone. A score can be valid for one purpose and weak for another.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Limits</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Scores compare you to a <b>norm group</b>, a sample of people tested to set the averages. Old norms can be out of date.</li>\n<li>Average scores on such tests rose over the 20th century in many countries (the Flynn effect). This is one reason tests are re-normed.</li>\n<li>Language, schooling, test anxiety, tiredness and health can all shift a score.</li>\n<li>A score describes performance on certain tasks. It is not the whole worth or potential of a person.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"muted\">Real reliability values are listed in each test's manual. The numbers on this page are examples.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"p-qz\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"t-qz\" class=\"hidden\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<h2>Quick test</h2>\n<p>Your first answer to each question counts. <span class=\"val\" id=\"qscore\" aria-live=\"polite\">0 / 8</span></p>\n<div id=\"quiz\"></div>\n<p><button class=\"btn alt\" id=\"qreset\">↺ Reset quiz</button></p>\n</div>\n</section>\n</main>\n\n<script>\n(function(){\nconst $=id=>document.getElementById(id);\nconst SD=15;\n/* tabs */\nconst tabs=[$('t-num'),$('t-gr'),$('t-qz')];\nfunction sel(t){tabs.forEach(b=>{const on=b===t;b.setAttribute('aria-selected',on);b.tabIndex=on?0:-1;$(b.getAttribute('aria-controls')).classList.toggle('hidden',!on)});if(t.id==='t-gr')sim(false);}\ntabs.forEach((b,i)=>{b.onclick=()=>sel(b);b.onkeydown=e=>{let j=null;if(e.key==='ArrowRight')j=(i+1)%3;if(e.key==='ArrowLeft')j=(i+2)%3;if(j!==null){e.preventDefault();tabs[j].focus();sel(tabs[j]);}}});\n\n/* numerize */\nconst NS='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';\nfunction el(n,a,p){const e=document.createElementNS(NS,n);for(const k in a)e.setAttribute(k,a[k]);if(p)p.appendChild(e);return e}\nconst W=600,H=190,L=20,R=580,B=150,T=15;\nconst xs=v=>L+(v-40)/120*(R-L);\nconst pdf=v=>Math.exp(-((v-100)/SD)**2/2);\nfunction curve(score,lo,hi,ts){\n const s=$('curve');[...s.querySelectorAll(':not(desc)')].forEach(n=>n.remove());\n let d='M'+xs(40)+' '+B;for(let v=40;v<=160;v+=1)d+=' L'+xs(v).toFixed(1)+' '+(B-pdf(v)*(B-T)).toFixed(1);d+=' L'+xs(160)+' '+B+' Z';\n const a=Math.max(40,lo),b=Math.min(160,hi);\n el('rect',{x:xs(a),y:T,width:Math.max(0,xs(b)-xs(a)),height:B-T,fill:'var(--band)'},s);\n el('path',{d,fill:'none',stroke:'var(--muted)','stroke-width':2},s);\n el('line',{x1:L,x2:R,y1:B,y2:B,stroke:'var(--muted)'},s);\n for(let v=40;v<=160;v+=15){el('line',{x1:xs(v),x2:xs(v),y1:B,y2:B+5,stroke:'var(--muted)'},s);const t=el('text',{x:xs(v),y:B+20,'text-anchor':'middle','font-size':13,fill:'var(--muted)'},s);t.textContent=v;}\n el('line',{x1:xs(ts),x2:xs(ts),y1:T,y2:B,stroke:'var(--acc2)','stroke-width':2,'stroke-dasharray':'5 4'},s);\n el('line',{x1:xs(score),x2:xs(score),y1:T,y2:B,stroke:'var(--acc)','stroke-width':3},s);\n const t=el('text',{x:Math.min(R-60,Math.max(L+60,xs(score))),y:B+38,'text-anchor':'middle','font-size':13,fill:'var(--fg)'},s);\n t.textContent='Blue: observed · Orange dashed: est. true · Shade: range';\n}\nfunction num(){\n const x=+$('sc').value,r=+$('rel').value,z=+$('conf').value;\n $('scv').textContent=x;$('relv').textContent=r.toFixed(2);\n const sem=SD*Math.sqrt(1-r),lo=x-z*sem,hi=x+z*sem;\n const ts=100+r*(x-100),see=SD*Math.sqrt(r*(1-r));\n $('o-sem').textContent=sem.toFixed(1)+' points';\n $('o-band').textContent=Math.round(lo)+' – '+Math.round(hi);\n $('o-true').textContent=ts.toFixed(1);\n $('o-band2').textContent=Math.round(ts-z*see)+' – '+Math.round(ts+z*see);\n curve(x,lo,hi,ts);\n}\n['sc','rel','conf'].forEach(i=>$(i).addEventListener('input',num));\nfunction diff(){\n const a=+$('ia').value,b=+$('ib').value,ra=+$('ra').value,rb=+$('rb').value;\n $('rav').textContent=ra.toFixed(2);$('rbv').textContent=rb.toFixed(2);\n if(isNaN(a)||isNaN(b)){$('d-res').textContent='Enter two scores';return}\n const sed=SD*Math.sqrt(2-ra-rb),crit=1.96*sed,g=a-b;\n $('d-gap').textContent=(g>0?'+':'')+g;\n $('d-crit').textContent='± '+crit.toFixed(1);\n $('d-res').textContent=Math.abs(g)>=crit?'Bigger than error alone':'Could be just error';\n}\n['ia','ib','ra','rb'].forEach(i=>$(i).addEventListener('input',diff));\nnum();diff();\n\n/* graph */\nfunction rn(){let u=0,v=0;while(!u)u=Math.random();while(!v)v=Math.random();return Math.sqrt(-2*Math.log(u))*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*v)}\nfunction corr(a,b){const n=a.length;let ma=0,mb=0;for(let i=0;i<n;i++){ma+=a[i];mb+=b[i]}ma/=n;mb/=n;let sab=0,sa=0,sb=0;for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const da=a[i]-ma,db=b[i]-mb;sab+=da*db;sa+=da*da;sb+=db*db}return sab/Math.sqrt(sa*sb)}\nconst N=2000;let noise=null;\nfunction newNoise(){noise=[];for(let i=0;i<N;i++)noise.push([rn(),rn(),rn(),rn(),rn()])}\nconst band=v=>v<85?0:v<115?1:2;\nfunction cssv(n){return getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(n).trim()}\nfunction plot(cv,X,Y,diag,xl,yl){\n const w=cv.clientWidth||300,dpr=window.devicePixelRatio||1,h=w;\n cv.width=w*dpr;cv.height=h*dpr;cv.style.height=h+'px';\n const c=cv.getContext('2d');c.setTransform(dpr,0,0,dpr,0,0);c.clearRect(0,0,w,h);\n const pl=34,pb=30,pt=8,pr=8,iw=w-pl-pr,ih=h-pt-pb;\n const px=v=>pl+(v-40)/120*iw,py=v=>pt+ih-(v-40)/120*ih;\n c.strokeStyle=cssv('--grid');c.fillStyle=cssv('--muted');c.font='11px system-ui';c.lineWidth=1;\n for(let v=40;v<=160;v+=30){c.beginPath();c.moveTo(px(v),pt);c.lineTo(px(v),pt+ih);c.moveTo(pl,py(v));c.lineTo(pl+iw,py(v));c.stroke();c.textAlign='center';c.fillText(v,px(v),h-pb+14);c.textAlign='right';c.fillText(v,pl-4,py(v)+4)}\n c.textAlign='center';c.fillText(xl,pl+iw/2,h-3);\n c.save();c.translate(10,pt+ih/2);c.rotate(-Math.PI/2);c.fillText(yl,0,0);c.restore();\n if(diag){c.strokeStyle=cssv('--acc2');c.setLineDash([5,4]);c.lineWidth=2;c.beginPath();c.moveTo(px(40),py(40));c.lineTo(px(160),py(160));c.stroke();c.setLineDash([])}\n c.fillStyle=cssv('--acc');c.globalAlpha=.35;\n for(let i=0;i<X.length;i++){const x=X[i],y=Y[i];if(x<40||x>160||y<40||y>160)continue;c.beginPath();c.arc(px(x),py(y),2,0,6.283);c.fill()}\n c.globalAlpha=1;\n}\nfunction sim(fresh){\n if(fresh||!noise)newNoise();\n const r=+$('g-r').value,v=+$('g-v').value,ry=+$('g-y').value;\n $('g-rv').textContent=r.toFixed(2);$('g-vv').textContent=v.toFixed(2);$('g-yv').textContent=ry.toFixed(2);\n const sr=Math.sqrt(r),se=Math.sqrt(1-r),sv=Math.sqrt(1-v*v),sy=Math.sqrt(ry),sye=Math.sqrt(1-ry);\n const X1=[],X2=[],Y=[];let ch=0,hi=0,hiBoth=0;\n for(let i=0;i<N;i++){const[t,e1,e2,u,e3]=noise[i];\n  const a=Math.round(100+SD*(sr*t+se*e1)),b=Math.round(100+SD*(sr*t+se*e2));\n  const y=100+SD*(sy*(v*t+sv*u)+sye*e3);\n  X1.push(a);X2.push(b);Y.push(y);\n  if(band(a)!==band(b))ch++;if(a>=130){hi++;if(b>=130)hiBoth++}}\n $('s-rr').textContent=corr(X1,X2).toFixed(2);\n $('s-cat').textContent=(ch/N*100).toFixed(1)+'%';\n $('s-130').textContent=hi?Math.round(hiBoth/hi*100)+'% ('+hiBoth+' of '+hi+')':'none';\n const ov=corr(X1,Y);$('s-val').textContent=ov.toFixed(2);\n $('s-exp').textContent=(v*sr*sy).toFixed(2);\n if($('p-gr').classList.contains('hidden'))return;\n plot($('c1'),X1,X2,true,'First test','Retest');\n plot($('c2'),X1,Y,false,'Test score','Outcome');\n $('c1').setAttribute('aria-label','Scatter plot of first test against retest. Correlation '+corr(X1,X2).toFixed(2)+'.');\n $('c2').setAttribute('aria-label','Scatter plot of test score against outcome. Correlation '+ov.toFixed(2)+'.');\n}\n['g-r','g-v','g-y'].forEach(i=>$(i).addEventListener('input',()=>sim(false)));\n$('g-new').onclick=()=>sim(true);\nlet rt;window.addEventListener('resize',()=>{clearTimeout(rt);rt=setTimeout(()=>sim(false),150)});\nif(window.matchMedia)matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').addEventListener('change',()=>sim(false));\n\n/* quiz */\nconst Q=[\n ['What does reliability mean?',['The score measures the right thing','The score is consistent across tries and items','The score is high'],1,'Reliability is about consistency. Measuring the right thing is validity.'],\n ['What does validity mean?',['The test is long','Scores are the same every time','The score supports the use you make of it'],2,'Validity asks: does this score really tell us what we want to know, for this purpose?'],\n ['A score is 100 and the SEM is 3. What is the 95% range, roughly?',['97 – 103','94 – 106','85 – 115'],1,'1.96 × 3 ≈ 6, so 100 ± 6 gives about 94 to 106.'],\n ['If reliability goes up, the SEM…',['goes down','goes up','stays the same'],0,'SEM = 15 × √(1 − reliability). More reliability means less error.'],\n ['Someone scores 135. On a retest, what is most likely?',['Exactly 135 again','A bit closer to 100','Much higher'],1,'Part of an extreme score is luck. On retest, scores tend to drift toward the average.'],\n ['Can a test be reliable but not valid?',['Yes','No'],0,'A scale that is always 2 kg off is consistent, but wrong. Consistency alone is not enough.'],\n ['Why are combined scores usually more reliable than single subtests?',['They use harder items','They are based on more items, so random errors cancel out more','They are scored by computers'],1,'More items means random ups and downs average out.'],\n ['Two index scores differ by more than the 95% “gap needed”. What can you say?',['The gap is rare in the population','The person has a disorder','The gap is probably not just measurement error'],2,'It means error alone is unlikely to explain it. It does not mean the gap is rare or that something is wrong.']\n];\nconst ans=new Array(Q.length).fill(null);\nfunction score(){$('qscore').textContent=ans.filter(a=>a===true).length+' / '+Q.length}\nfunction build(){\n const box=$('quiz');box.innerHTML='';\n Q.forEach((q,i)=>{\n  const fs=document.createElement('fieldset');\n  const lg=document.createElement('legend');lg.textContent=(i+1)+'. '+q[0];fs.appendChild(lg);\n  q[1].forEach((o,j)=>{const lb=document.createElement('label');lb.className='opt';\n   const r=document.createElement('input');r.type='radio';r.name='q'+i;r.value=j;\n   r.addEventListener('change',()=>{const ok=j===q[2];if(ans[i]===null){ans[i]=ok;score()}\n    fb.className='fb '+(ok?'ok':'bad');fb.textContent=(ok?'✅ Correct. ':'❌ Not quite. ')+q[3]});\n   lb.appendChild(r);const s=document.createElement('span');s.textContent=o;lb.appendChild(s);fs.appendChild(lb)});\n  const fb=document.createElement('div');fb.className='fb';fb.setAttribute('aria-live','polite');fs.appendChild(fb);\n  box.appendChild(fs)});\n}\n$('qreset').onclick=()=>{ans.fill(null);build();score()};\nbuild();score();\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>",
